"\n\n\n\n\n\n## Ordered\n\n\n\n## Review\nThere are so many types of makguksu out there, but the deulmak (perilla seed makguksu) here was a style I hadn't tried much before.  \n\nThe buckwheat itself already has a nutty aroma, and on top of that it's loaded with ground perilla seed powder, so the nuttiness is maximized — combined with a subtle sweetness, it's a flavor even kids would enjoy.  \nIt's mild and smooth rather than pungent, so I think people of all ages could enjoy it without any trouble.  \n\nThe portion can feel a bit small, so I'd definitely recommend getting the large size.  \nFor a side dish, it looked like most people were ordering the mandu (dumplings).\n\nIf you're expecting an icy, chilled makguksu, you might be a little disappointed, but if you already enjoy the perilla oil makguksu style, you'll definitely love this one.  \n\nThere's usually a wait on weekends, but the restaurant has plenty of seating and it's the kind of meal people finish quickly, so you likely won't have to wait too long.  \n\nThere is a dedicated parking lot, but it doesn't have many spots.  \nThere's also a public parking lot nearby, but on weekends it's likely to be full.  \nParking here always seems to be a bit of a struggle on weekends.  \n\n## Pictures\n\n\n\n\n\n"